{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And HaShem was with Joseph, and he was a successful man, and he was in the house of his master the Egyptian.</b> Scripture mentions 'וַיְהִי' three times, because Joseph ascended three rungs, one after the other, and afterwards his master also gave him three kinds of authority corresponding to the increase in success that he saw in him; therefore he added to him authority twofold and threefold. For at first, 'וַיְהִי ה׳ אֶת יוֹסֵף' — He was with him alone, and his success had not yet extended to others. And afterwards, 'וַיְהִי אִישׁ מַצְלִיחַ' — to others, for 'מַצְלִיחַ' is an active causative: he caused success also for his master, until HaShem was also with his master. And afterwards, 'וַיְהִי בְּבֵית אֲדֹנָיו' — HaShem was also among the members of his master's household. And so closely did success cling to Joseph's heels, that from Joseph it extended to his master, and from his master to the rest of the members of his household who dwelt with his master. It turns out that his master too brought success to others. 'וַיַּרְא אֲדֹנָיו כִּי ה׳ אִתּוֹ' — that is, literally with him, to this extraordinary degree, so that 'כָּל אֲשֶׁר הוּא עֹשֶׂה' — meaning what the master does — 'ה׳ מַצְלִיחַ בְּיָדוֹ', for from him the success extended also to the members of his household, because HaShem was with him together with the master. Therefore 'וַיִּמְצָא יוֹסֵף חֵן בְּעֵינָיו וַיְשָׁרֶת אֹתוֹ וַיַּפְקִדֵהוּ עַל בֵּיתוֹ' — he made him officer over all the members of his household, because from Joseph the success came to them. 'וְכָל אֲשֶׁר יֶשׁ לוֹ נָתַן בְּיָדוֹ', for from Joseph the success came upon all that he has."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:32.114731273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}